"""Frozen reference-only and framing setup prompts."""
SELECTION_PROMPT = 'Describe the photograph\'s framing, then classify it for extracting a COMPLETE isolated fashion product.\nChoose ONE view label:\nFLAT_LAY: whole product(s) alone on a surface, with their outside outline visible.\nPRODUCT_ONLY: whole product(s) alone, e.g. hanging or invisible mannequin.\nWORN: any actual person or body part wearing, holding or modelling the item. Printed portraits on fabric are not actual people.\nDETAIL: fabric texture fills the frame, or only a subsection such as a neckline, sleeve, fastening or hem is shown. A fabric rectangle is NOT a whole garment. Close-up detail shots never count as flatlays.\nOTHER: visible mannequin, unrelated scene or uncertain.\nFor FLAT_LAY or PRODUCT_ONLY, list the visible product types in items. For any clothing garment include the word "clothing" (so the entire garment, including all attached layers, can be segmented), plus its plain type, such as "dress", "shirt", "vest". For jewellery, shoes or bags use those specific object names. List ALL items of a pair/set. For WORN, DETAIL or OTHER items must be [].\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with exactly these keys: description (a brief explanation of visible framing), view (one label above), items (list of strings).'

FRAMING_PROMPT = 'The first image is a product-only reference. The second image is the worn photograph to classify. Judge the framing of the second image relative to the product in the first. OVERVIEW: most of the referenced product is visible, even if the person\'s head or feet are cropped, or the view is from behind. A whole bikini, shoe or shirt on a cropped person counts as overview. DETAIL: the photo is magnified into only a small fragment of that product and crops away most of it. Return JSON only: {"role":"overview"} or {"role":"detail"}.'

NAMING_PROMPT = 'This is an isolated product photograph. Name the visible product using garment nouns. Choose from: top, shirt, blouse, T-shirt, sweater, hoodie, jacket, coat, vest, dress, pants, shorts, skirt, bodysuit, bikini top, bikini bottom, swimsuit, shoes, bag. Select only the product types actually shown; attached draping belongs to its garment. Never answer clothing, clothes, garment or apparel. Return JSON only: {"queries":["specific product noun"]}.'
